  "id": "posttest-only-control-group-design",
  "term": "posttest-only control-group design",
  "definition": "A posttest-only control-group design is a study design in which separate groups are compared only after an intervention or condition, without measuring them beforehand. In the source packet, it is described as a static group comparison used to compare outcomes across groups after different subtitle conditions.",
